0000:                   *  COPYRIGHT (C) 1987 by Peter Durham
0000:                   *    Permission is given to all members of the OS-9 community to use,
0000:                   *    modify, and share this program for their personal enjoyment.
0000:                   *    Commercial use of this program, which was written for fun to share with
0000:                   *    the community, is prohibited without the consent of the author.
0000:                   *    Please share any extensions or modifications with the author, who
0000:                   *    would be interested in hearing about them.
0000:                   * Small optimizations for size by L. Curtis Boyle 11/26/2017
0000:                   *
0000:                   *  NOTE
0000:                   *    Quick poll... how does the above sound as a copyright notice?  Clearly,
0000:                   *    authors like to share their work while maintaining some control on it.
0000:                   *    And it doesn't seem fair for someone else to make $ from something
0000:                   *    someone else made for fun.  I think the above conditions are what most
0000:                   *    people want.  Let me know what you think.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *  NOTE
0000:                   *    The inspiration for this utility was the os9p3 example in
0000:                   *    the Tandy Level 2 manual.  Tandy deserves praise for
0000:                   *    including examples such as this one in their manuals.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *  NOTE
0000:                   *    There is something funny about KrnP3 modules... some versions
0000:                   *    are not liked, others are.  When developing this module, often
0000:                   *    a version would fail... but if I added a "leas 0,s" right before
0000:                   *    the "rts" in PrinBuf, it would work!  Probably the location and
0000:                   *    operation are not significant.  This version here has never failed
0000:                   *    to boot on my system; however, if it does on yours (or you change
0000:                   *    it), try putting such things in.
0000:                   *
0000:                   *  NOTE
0000:                   *    For those people who just can't have enough... KrnP3 will look for
0000:                   *    a module called KrnP4, and link to it, and execute it.  Thanks to
0000:                   *    Kev for this idea.  Now we can keep additions to the kernel in nice
0000:                   *    separate chunks.  (How long 'til KrnP11 comes around...?)
0000:                   *
0000:                   * Edt/Rev  YYYY/MM/DD  Modified by
0000:                   * Comment
0000:                   * ------------------------------------------------------------------
0000:                   *   1      1987/06/23  Peter E. Durham
0000:                   * First release.
0000:                   *   2      2017/11/26  L. Curtis Boyle
0000:                   *          Speed and size optimizations
0000:                   *
0000:                   *   3      2018/01/26  L. Curtis Boyle
0000:                   *          More speed optimizations (MoveBuf only copies 15 bytes,not 80,
0000:                   *          since it never needs more than that, and other minor mods.) Also
0000:                   *          shrank it some more.
0000:                   
0000:                            nam   krnp3
0000:                            ttl   Printerr functionality for Level 2
0000:                   
0000:                            ifp1
0000:                            use   defsfile
0000:                            endc  
0000:                   
00C0:                   Type     set   Systm      ;System module, 6809 object code
0081:                   atrv     set   ReEnt+rev
0001:                   rev      set   1
0003:                   edition  set   3
0000:                   
0000: 87CD0120000DC081           mod   eom,name,Type,atrv,Entry,256
0009: 001D0100
0000:                   
000D: 4B726E50B3        name     fcs   "KrnP3"
0012: 03                         fcb   edition
0013:                   
0013: 0F                SvcTbl   fcb   F$PErr     ;System call number
0014: 0032                       fdb   PErr-*-2   ;Offset to code
0016: 80                         fcb   $80        ;End of table
0017:                   
0017: 6B726E7034        P4Name   fcc   "krnp4"
001C: 0D                         fcb   C$CR
001D:                   
001D:                   *+
001D:                   *  Initialization routine and table
001D:                   *-
001D: 318CF3            Entry    leay  SvcTbl,pcr ;Get address of table
0020: 103F32                     os9   F$SSvc     ;Install services in table
0023: 86C0                       lda   #Type      ;Get system module type for KrnP4
0025: 308CEF                     leax  P4Name,pcr ;Get name for KrnP4
0028: 103F00                     os9   F$Link     ;Try to link to it
002B: 257C                       bcs   PErrBye    ;If not found, exit
002D: 6EA4                       jmp   ,y         ;Execute it, return from there
002F:                   
002F:                   *+
002F:                   *  The new F$Perr service call
002F:                   *-
002F:                   *+
002F:                   *  Data (in user space!) - reserved in users stack. 89 bytes
002F:                   *-
0050:                   BufLen   equ   80
0000:                   Buf      rmb   BufLen
0007:                   HunDig   equ   Buf+7
0008:                   TenDig   equ   Buf+8
0009:                   OneDig   equ   Buf+9
0050:                   DataMem  equ   .
0050:                   
002F: 4572726F72202330  ErrMsg   fcc   "Error #000"
0038: 30
000A:                   ErrLen   equ   *-ErrMsg
0039:                   
0039: 2F64642F7379732F  FilNam   fcc   "/dd/sys/errmsg"
0042: 72726D7367
0047: 0D                         fcb   C$CR
000F:                   FilLen   equ   *-FilNam
0048:                   
0048:                   *+
0048:                   *  FUNCTION     PErr
0048:                   *  PURPOSE      Top level routine
0048:                   *  REGISTERS    B = Error code (after Setup)
0048:                   *               U = User memory area (after Setup)
0048:                   *               Y = User process descriptor (after Setup)
0048:                   *               A = Error file path number (after OpenFil)
0048:                   *               X = Pointer to strings
0048:                   *-
0048: E642              PErr     ldb   R$B,u      ;Get error code
004A: 109E50                     ldy   D.Proc     ;Get user's process descriptor
004D: EE24                       ldu   P$SP,y     ;Get user's stack pointer
004F: 33C9FFB0                   leau  -DataMem,u ;Reserve a little space (89 bytes) to build string
0053: 308CD9                     leax  ErrMsg,pcr ;Get pointer to "Error #000"
0056: 8D52                       bsr   MoveBuf    ;Go copy it over
0058: 8D61                       bsr   WritNum    ;Go copy the number into it
005A: 3430                       pshs  x,y        ;Save regs
005C: A6A832                     lda   P$Path+2,y ;Get Std Err path
005F: 3040                       leax  Buf,u      ;Get ptr to message
0061: 108E000A                   ldy   #ErrLen    ;Maximum ErrLen characters to print
0065: 103F8A                     os9   I$Write    ;Write out Error message
0068: 3530                       puls  x,y        ;Restore regs
006A: 253D                       bcs   PErrBye    ;If error, abort
006C: 308CCA                     leax  FilNam,pcr ;Get pointer to "/dd/sys/errmsg"
006F:                   * Tried skipping copy to Buf, but does not work
006F:                   *  and using direct ptr
006F: 8D39                       bsr   MoveBuf    ;Go copy it over
0071: 8601                       lda   #READ.     ;Open path for read access
0073: 3040                       leax  Buf,u      ;Get ptr to string
0075: 103F84                     os9   I$Open     ;Open errmsg file
0078: 252F                       bcs   PErrBye    ;If couldn't open, abort
007A: 3420              Loop     pshs  y          ;Save users prc dsc ptr
007C: 3040                       leax  Buf,u      ;Point to buffer
007E: 108E0050                   ldy   #BufLen    ;Maximum BufLen characters to read
0082: 103F8B                     os9   I$ReadLn   ;Read a line
0085: 3520                       puls  y          ;Restore reg
0087: 250E                       bcs   Error      ;If error, print CR, and abort
0089: 3404                       pshs  b          ;Save error code
008B: 8D5F                       bsr   CalcNum    ;What number is on this line?
008D: E1E4                       cmpb  ,s         ;Is this line the right line?
008F: 3504                       puls  b          ;Restore error code
0091: 26E7                       bne   Loop       ;If not right line, loop again
0093: 8D7A                       bsr   PrinBuf    ;If right line, write line out
0095: 200F                       bra   Close      ;Done, so close the file
0097:                   
0097:                   * should be able to only preserve A (path to errmsg file)
0097: 3402              Error    pshs  a          ;Save path to errmsg file
0099: E626                       ldb   P$Task,y   ;Get user task number
009B: 860D                       lda   #C$CR      ;Load A with a CR
009D: 3040                       leax  Buf,u      ;Get pointer to buffer
009F: 103F4A                     os9   F$STABX    ;Move the CR to the buffer
00A2: 8D6B                       bsr   PrinBuf    ;Go print it
00A4: 3502                       puls  a          ;Restore path to errmsg file
00A6: 103F8F            Close    os9   I$Close    ;Close the file
00A9: 39                PErrBye  rts              ;Return from system call
00AA:                   
00AA:                   *+
00AA:                   *  FUNCTION     MoveBuf
00AA:                   *  PURPOSE      Copies string to user space
00AA:                   *  TAKES        X = location of string in system space
00AA:                   *-
00AA: 3466              MoveBuf  pshs  u,y,d      ;Save registers
00AC: 96D0                       lda   D.SysTsk   ;Get system process task number
00AE: E626                       ldb   P$Task,y   ;Get user process task number
00B0: 3340                       leau  Buf,u      ;Get pointer to destination buffer
00B2: 108E000F                   ldy   #FilLen    ;Copy 15 bytes over max (longest)
00B6: 103F38                     os9   F$Move     ;Move string to user space
00B9: 35E6                       puls  d,y,u,pc   ;Restore registers and return
00BB:                   
00BB:                   *+
00BB:                   *  FUNCTION     WriteNum
00BB:                   *  PURPOSE      Puts the ASCII value of the error code in user space
00BB:                   *  TAKES        B = error code
00BB:                   *-
00BB: 3416              WritNum  pshs  x,d        ;Save registers
00BD: 4F                         clra             ;Start A as 0
00BE: C164              Huns     cmpb  #100       ;Is B >= 100?
00C0: 2505                       blo   HunDone    ;If not, go do Tens
00C2: 4C                         inca             ;Increment hundreds digit
00C3: C064                       subb  #100       ;Subtract 100 from B
00C5: 20F7                       bra   Huns       ;Go do again
00C7:                   
00C7: 3047              HunDone  leax  HunDig,u   ;Where to put digit
00C9: 8D16                       bsr   WritDig    ;Go put it there
00CB: 4F                         clra             ;Start A again as 0
00CC: C10A              Tens     cmpb  #10        ;Is B >= 10?
00CE: 2505                       blo   TenDone    ;If not, go do Ones
00D0: 4C                         inca             ;Increment hundreds digit
00D1: C00A                       subb  #10        ;Subtract 10 from B
00D3: 20F7                       bra   Tens       ;Go do again
00D5:                   
00D5: 3048              TenDone  leax  TenDig,u   ;Where to put digit
00D7: 8D08                       bsr   WritDig    ;Go put it there
00D9: 1F98                       tfr   b,a        ;Get ones digit
00DB: 3049                       leax  OneDig,u   ;Where to put digit
00DD: 8D02                       bsr   WritDig    ;Go put it there
00DF: 3596                       puls  d,x,pc     ;Restore registers and return
00E1:                   
00E1:                   *+
00E1:                   *  FUNCTION     WritDig
00E1:                   *  PURPOSE      Copy digit into user space
00E1:                   *  TAKES        A = digit to copy (not in ASCII yet)
00E1:                   *               X = where to put digit
00E1: 3404              WritDig  pshs  b          ;Save working byte
00E3: 8B30                       adda  #'0        ;Convert A to ASCII
00E5: E626                       ldb   P$Task,y   ;Get task number
00E7: 103F4A                     os9   F$STABX    ;Write that digit to user space
00EA: 3584                       puls  b,pc       ;Restore registers and return
00EC:                   
00EC:                   *+
00EC:                   *  FUNCTION     CalcNum
00EC:                   *  PURPOSE      Converts ASCII number in user space to binary
00EC:                   *  TAKES        Buf (in user space) = ASCII number
00EC:                   *  GIVES        B = number converted
00EC:                   *               X = points to first nonnumeric character
00EC:                   *-
00EC: 3402              CalcNum  pshs  a          ;Save register
00EE: 3040                       leax  Buf,u      ;Get pointer to buffer
00F0: 5F                         clrb             ;Clear result to 0 to start
00F1: 3404              NextDig  pshs  b          ;Save current result
00F3: E626                       ldb   P$Task,y   ;Get user process task #
00F5: 103F49                     os9   F$LDABX    ;Get digit from user space
00F8: 3504                       puls  b          ;Get current result back
00FA: 8030                       suba  #'0        ;Convert to binary; is it less than zero?
00FC: 2B0F                       bmi   CalcBye    ;If so, return
00FE: 8109                       cmpa  #9         ;Is the digit more than nine?
0100: 220B                       bhi   CalcBye    ;If so, return
0102: 3402                       pshs  a          ;Save the digit while we multiply
0104: 860A                       lda   #10        ;Multiply current number by 10
0106: 3D                         mul              ;Do it
0107: EBE0                       addb  ,s+        ;Add new digit to number
0109: 3001                       leax  1,x        ;Advance X to next digit
010B: 20E4                       bra   NextDig    ;Go get the next digit
010D:                            
010D: 3582              CalcBye  puls  a,pc       ;Restore register and return
010F:                   
010F:                   *+
010F:                   *  FUNCTION     PrinBuf
010F:                   *  PURPOSE      Prints out the string from user space
010F:                   *  TAKES        X (in user space) = String to print
010F:                   *-
010F: 3422              PrinBuf  pshs  y,a        ;Save registers
0111: A6A832                     lda   P$Path+2,y ;Get StdErr path number
0114: 108E0050                   ldy   #BufLen    ;Maximum BufLen characters to print
0118: 103F8C                     os9   I$WritLn   ;Write out message
011B: 35A2                       puls  a,y,pc     ;Restore registers and return
011D:                            
011D: 029EAB                     emod  
0120:                   eom      equ   *
0120:                            end   
0 Pass 2 errors.

